GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "3F80B4EC13FDA5D5"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aMissionEvents + {
    GC_Event "{EDE34E86A6533F41}" {
     m_sName "time (event 6, 3000s)"
     m_Advanced GC_EventOptions "{0ACAE97B6D827653}" {
      m_fDelay 3000
     }
     m_aActions {
      GC_MessageAction "{6227CA95FFE17D31}" {
       m_sTitle "Time Limit Reached"
       m_sMessage "If OPFOR has not captured the town yet, they lose."
      }
     }
    }
    GC_Event "{5076C93B8592CD21}" {
     m_sName "time (event 6, 2700s)"
     m_Advanced GC_EventOptions "{EF6AB398DEFA170E}" {
      m_fDelay 2700
     }
     m_aActions {
      GC_MessageAction "{19B0D298872BA278}" {
       m_sTitle "5 Minutes Remaining"
       m_sMessage ""
      }
     }
    }
   }
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{A191E27EE2A41D7B}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "Last night our company conducted a raid and destroyed a battery of 2S1 Self Propelled Howitzers. Our withdrawal was disrupted by enemy artillery fire and our platoon was left sheltering in town while the rest of the company set up defensive positions in the forest to our north west."\
     ""\
     "The barrage has ceased but with only 15 minutes of darkness remaining the company commander has ordered us to hold our position and protect the company's eastern flank from likely advancing soviet forces for 50 minutes, at which point we can call on our air support and enable our withdrawal."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{090D78FE6D5703DE}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "Scenario Overview"
     m_sContent "Soviet BTR Company assault a Platoon of British Paratroopers."
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{65F76B287E80812E}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "Last night a battery of the Regiment's 2S1 Self Propelled Howitzers came under attack. Their last radio transmission reported contact in the town to their north but we have heard nothing since. Our battalion has been tasked to find, fix and destroy the enemy force. "\
     ""\
     "Our company has been assigned the task of securing Objective Boris and the gun positions in order to set the conditions for the remainder of the battalion to clear the forest. Our preparatory barrage in the town has stopped, signalling the beginning of our assault. First light is in 15 minutes."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{50EA07FE1838160D}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Situation Enemy"
     m_sContent "We are expecting a soviet motor rifle company mounted in BTR's to conduct a counter attack from the south. They will be wearing tan uniforms with AK74, RPK, RPG and under barrel grenade launchers with mobile fire support from their BTRs."\
     ""\
     "Their mostly likely mission will be to recapture their gun pits and possibly Objective Marble."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{2B0F57870621E812}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "Mission Notes"
     m_sContent "Time Limit: 50 Min"\
     ""\
     ""\
     "OPFOR Victory: USSR Secure the Town Objective and both Gun Pit Objectives OR"\
     "90% of Blufor are killed"\
     ""\
     "Blufor Victory: 70% of OPFOR are killed OR Blufor retains the Town Objective at 50 minute time limit."\
     ""\
     "2 min capture timer on the trenches, 5 min capture timer on the town."\
     "Retaking objectives is not possible. "\
     ""\
     "All sides take note: there will be 15 minutes of darkness until the sun rises, keep this in mind when route planning."
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{3437D9862552D4E2}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Situation Enemy"
     m_sContent "Enemy forces are likely to be elite, light infantry operating in platoon to company strength. They will likely be well armed and motivated, but should be battered and disorganized from the barrage."\
     ""\
     "If they have not already slipped away, they will likely be in the process of retreating north west into the forest. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{503E300BC640BDC1}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "Situation Friendly"
     m_sContent "The rest of the company has established an ambush and blocking position to our west, leaving us the task of guarding our eastern flank."\
     ""\
     "As the rearguard, we have a platoon of infantry at 033 035, with additional anti tank weapons from the rest of the company. We also have two captured AGS systems we've deployed to guard our flank. 2nd Platoon has given us two sections (AI) to defend each trench line, and we have been given two attached LP/OP teams (Players)."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{DD8D11C2B436E062}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Situation Friendly"
     m_sContent "You have a company of BTR mounted infantry at 030 020. Each platoon has 3x BTR-70s and the company commander has one as well. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{0FB7CDB20E8847D2}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "21 Platoon will delay enemy forces in grid 03 03 for 50 minutes in order to prevent the company's encirclement."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{D2D64BA2724315B1}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "210 Company will secure Objective Boris and both gun positions within 50 minutes in order to provide security for the rest of the battalion."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CDBD84A22CE05B68}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "Execution"
     m_sContent "Company wants us to utilize successive defensive positions in depth to disrupt their deployment and attack. Withdraw as necessary and avoid becoming decisively engaged as long as possible."\
     ""\
     "End state is 21 Platoon at Objective Marble, ready to conduct the withdrawal, in 50 minutes."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{3715E25233123D24}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "Execution"
     m_sContent "Battalion has ordered you to avoid the western approach which is covered by the forest, and not pursue the enemy in to it under any circumstances. "\
     ""\
     "Discretion is otherwise up to the CO."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{490A54CB690B2754}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "Service and Support"
     m_sContent "We have 1x Carl G per section and several M72s."\
     "We have 2x Captured AGS systems with some ammunition marked on your map."\
     "There are white, green and orange flares dispersed among the platoon but the sun will be rising shortly."\
     ""\
     "Platoon and Section leadership have radios."\
     ""\
     "Note: The OPs do not have radios and should return to friend lines when they have something to report, or if they are outflanked."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{EFBFA54D5E659BF9}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "Service and Support"
     m_sContent "Transport:"\
     "9x BTR-70 (seats 19 + 3 crew)"\
     ""\
     "There is extra ammunition inside the BTRs."\
     ""\
     "Portable radios are distributed to Coy and Platoon leadership. Squad level radios are in the BTRs."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{5340291B82D2814A}" {
     m_iOrder 14
     m_sTitle "Command and Signals"
     m_sContent "Succession of Command:"\
     ""\
     "21"\
     "21A"\
     "21B"\
     "21C"\
     "21D 21E"\
     "Platoon net: 48.0MHz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{70F27D77899B5EA6}" {
     m_iOrder 15
     m_sTitle "Command and Signals"
     m_sContent "Succession of Command:"\
     ""\
     "210 Coy Commander"\
     "->First Sergeant"\
     ""\
     "211 Platoon Leader"\
     "->Deputy Platoon Leader ->211 -> 212 -> 213"\
     ""\
     "214 Platoon Leader"\
     "->Deputy Platoon Leader ->214 -> 215 -> 216"\
     ""\
     "217 Platoon Leader"\
     "->Deputy Platoon Leader ->217 -> 218 -> 219"\
     ""\
     ""\
     "Company Net: 42.0MHz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{3C77EF8F83590779}" {
     m_iOrder 16
     m_sTitle "Mission Notes"
     m_sContent "Blue AO Limit is for the platoon."\
     "Green AO Limit is for the OP so they can conduct forward reconnaissance."\
     ""\
     "Note: Once a member of the OP team crosses back into the Blue AO Limit, they can no longer go back outside of it. "\
     ""\
     "OP teams spawns at different locations and have radio. They are meant to retreat into the Blue AO limit once they have information to pass on or out outflanked. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{E91D173849C458A8}" {
     m_iOrder 17
     m_sTitle "Mission Notes"
     m_sContent "The mission is meant to be a very simple attack, with the challenge coming from the soviet's lack of tools for maintaining command and control."\
     ""\
     "Platoon and Squad leaders need to know that the squad radios are kept in the BTR's. "\
     "Platoon leaders also need to choose a squad to ride with as they don't have their own BTR."\
     ""\
     "I recommend either keeping the vehicles organic or having someone remain in control of the BTR group if separated (i.e: Deputy Platoon Lead or First Sergeant, etc)."\
     ""\
     "Also consider using runners to communicate between the platoons when dismounted. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CCC16BF5FEA6AF25}" {
     m_iOrder 18
     m_sTitle "Capturing Objectives"
     m_sContent "Redfor must be in 90% control of their objectives for their respective capture times."\
     "It takes 2 minutes for each gun position, and 5 minutes for the town. "\
     ""\
     "Recapturing Objectives is not possible for Blufor, but they can reset the capture timer by entering the objective radius."\
     ""\
     "Radius are not marked to prevent meta-gaming but they fully encompass each feature."\
     ""\
     "There will be no messages to indicate capturing progress, the only message will appear when the Redfor has captured one."
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
